.he "umount (1)                   4/13/82                   umount (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd           
PROGRAM
.in +5
.br
.bd
umount 
- dismount a file system
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
USAGE
.in +5
.br
umount special
.br
umount directory
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
FUNCTION
.in +5
.br
The named special file is dismounted.
A directory may be named instead; it is looked up in /etc/mtab,
and then in /etc/fstab, to find the special file mounted there.

The special file must have been previously mounted
with the
.bd
mount
command.

It is not permitted to dismount a file system with files still open.
Diagnostic: "Device busy".

Sometimes it is necessary to use the "change directory" command 
before dismounting a device. As an example:
.sp
.ti +5
.bd
cd /; umount /dev/dja 
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
EXAMPLE
.in +5
.ti +5
.bd
umount /dev/dja

to dismount a floppy.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
mount(1) - to mount file systems








